  "$about": "The Node.js build Rosalena downloads when this PC has no Node.js of its own and the person installs OmniRoute (it is an npm package and runs on Node). DATA: src/node-runtime.mjs picks one asset by platform, checks its sha256 and unpacks it into ~/.rosalena/node, used only by Rosalena (nothing is added to the system PATH, no admin rights). Pinned on purpose: an LTS security release at least two weeks old, on the same major line as the OmniRoute copy measured working (Node 24; OmniRoute 3.8.52 accepts >=22.22.2 <23 || >=24 <27), with the digests from nodejs.org/dist/v24.22.1/SHASUMS256.txt.",
